  "answer_text": "Great question! The latest iPhone lineup includes the **iPhone 17, iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone 17 Pro Max, iPhone Air, and the newest iPhone 17e**. Here's where you can buy them:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcf1 Current iPhone Lineup\nApple's current flagship iPhone lineup includes the **iPhone 17e** (2026), **iPhone 17**, **iPhone 17 Pro**, **iPhone 17 Pro Max**, and **iPhone Air** (all 2025).\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udecd\ufe0f Where to Buy\n\n1. **Apple (apple.com or Apple Store)**\n   - Apple offers two-hour delivery from an Apple Store, free delivery, or easy pickup options.\n   - When you buy directly from Apple, you'll get access to **Personal Setup** \u2014 guided online sessions where a Specialist can walk you through setup and data transfer or help you explore new features.\n   - You can also trade in your current iPhone or Android device and apply any credit toward your purchase.\n\n2. **Best Buy (bestbuy.com)**\n   - Best Buy carries the latest Apple iPhones and accessories, including the newest iPhone models.\n   - You can look for trade-in discounts, coverage plan offers, or consider an unlocked iPhone for cellular plan flexibility.\n\n3. **T-Mobile (t-mobile.com)**\n   - T-Mobile carries the full current iPhone lineup, including the iPhone 17 Pro Max, iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone 17e, iPhone Air, and iPhone 17.\n\n4. **Other Carriers** (AT&T, Verizon, etc.) also typically carry the latest iPhones, often with trade-in deals and financing options.\n\n5. **Amazon** \u2014 You can also find iPhones on Amazon, including refurbished models at lower prices.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcb0 Price Range\n- The **iPhone 17e** is Apple's most affordable current option at **$599**, featuring the A19 chip, 256GB base storage, MagSafe charging, and a 48MP camera.\n- The **base iPhone 17** starts at **$799** and includes a 120Hz ProMotion display.\n- The **iPhone 17 Pro** starts at **$999**, sharing the same A19 Pro chip and camera system as the Pro Max in a more compact 6.3-inch size.\n\nWould you like help choosing which iPhone model is best for you?",
